cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aqlab in work you cite, please cite it as below."
title: "aqlab: any-locale, any-direction localization for Android APKs"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that localizes an Android application into any language at
  any text direction. It sets android:supportsRtl, migrates legacy left/right
  layout attributes to the logical start/end equivalents, scaffolds and applies a
  translation table from CLDR plural rules per locale (227 languages, 258 of them
  right-to-left), and lints string resources for Unicode bidirectional hazards,
  escaping bugs and format-specifier drift. Arabic is the hardest case and the one
  every check was built against. Single file, Python standard library only.
type: software
